        "title": "White-Collar Crime: Sutherland and Beyond",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "White-collar crime is crime committed by persons of respectability and high social status in the course of their occupations. Sutherland's 1939 presidential address to the American Sociological Association transformed criminology by showing that the focus on street crime was a systematic bias -- elite crime was larger in economic impact, under-prosecuted, and theoretically explained by the same mechanisms."
    }
